PRIVATE REFLECTION: {The opera is almost certainly Donizetti’s La Favorita (1840). Multiple colleagues (3,4,6,8) converge on the exact match: Alboni sang Leonora in the 1843 Scala revival; Caruso sang Fernando at the Met in 1905; the work then vanished from NY stages until the 1978 Met revival (73-year gap), the first NYC staging after Caruso. In that production the bass role (Baldassare) was sung by Bonaldo Giaiotti. 

Competing hypotheses (La Cenerentola 1997 with Dara/Alaimo; Semiramide 1990 with Ramey; Tancredi; 1950s Pinza revival) are weaker because they either ignore Caruso’s documented participation in this specific work or stretch the “first time … after Caruso was part of a Met production” clause. 

Key unresolved tension: whether “staged in New York City” strictly means main-stage Met or allows earlier touring/out-of-town Met performances. Evidence still favors La Favorita + Giaiotti. Need to confirm exact 1978 cast and any pre-1978 NYC history.}

